<DocPage eyebrow="DOCS / REFERENCE" title="Docs" lead="The guide explains how to complete a workflow. These API docs explain the classes, variables, functions, and ownership boundaries you encounter in source." description="Official Gua API and sample reference." section="docs">
  <Callout kind="tip" title="What Gua covers"><p>Gua keeps Playwright-like Semantic UI automation at its core, then provides game-development capabilities on the same protocol: the World Object Tree, gameplay input, MCP and WebMCP, AI agent exposure policy, virtual time, Recording, and visual comparison.</p></Callout>
  <Callout title="Source of truth"><p>The 1.1.0 feature and Value references link to source pinned to <code>gua-v1.1.0</code>. Existing API guides also link to implementation on <code>main</code>; package, engine, and archive support must be checked for the version in use.</p></Callout>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/release-1-1-0/"><span>GUA / 1.1.0</span><h3>1.1.0 feature reference</h3><p>Observe, Trace, Lint, Spatial, InputAction metadata, Timed Segment, distribution and support scope.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/value/"><span>VALUE / NPM</span><h3>Value v1 / gua-value-tools</h3><p>Shared typed values, validation, enum catalogs, and equality.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/dotnet-packages/"><span>PACKAGES / .NET</span><h3>.NET packages</h3><p>Core, Testing, Godot, Unity, Visual, Snapshots, Recording, and .NET Standard 2.1 support.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/gua-runtime/"><span>ADAPTER / RUNTIME</span><h3>Gua.Runtime guide</h3><p>Implement frames, actions, screenshots, and the Inspector bridge in a custom engine adapter.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/runtime-adapters/"><span>ENGINE / GODOT</span><h3>Godot API and specification</h3><p>The GDScript addon, GDExtension, external testing API, Control mappings, and extension boundary for other engines.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/unity-reference/"><span>ENGINE / UNITY</span><h3>Unity API and specification</h3><p>UPM, public types, control mappings, actions, test host, supported environment, and shared specification.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/github-actions/"><span>CI / GITHUB ACTIONS</span><h3>Gua Tester Actions</h3><p>Versioned Godot and Unity workflows for external Gua UI tests, diagnostics, and visual reports.</p></a>
    <a class="chapter-card" href="/docs/change-audit/"><span>CONTRIBUTING / AUDIT</span><h3>Change audit</h3><p>Run the read-only post-change gate or a cumulative pull-request audit with reproducible evidence.</p></a>
  </div>
  <h2>Guide or docs?</h2><div class="grid-2"><div class="mini-card"><strong>Guide</strong><p>Use it when you want to install, connect, and test Gua in sequence.</p></div><div class="mini-card"><strong>Docs</strong><p>Use it when you need the purpose or ownership of a specific type, variable, or function.</p></div></div>
</DocPage>
